      <h2>Safety</h2>
      <div class="warning">
        <strong>Read all safety warnings, instructions, illustrations and specifications supplied with the machine.</strong> The T-8 runs slowly and in water, which makes it one of the least hazardous machines in the shop, but it is still a power tool with a rotating abrasive wheel and a razor-sharp tool clamped to it.
      </div>
      <ul>
        <li>Operate the machine on a flat, stable surface in a clean, well-lit area. Keep children and bystanders away; make the workshop child-proof with padlocks or a master switch.</li>
        <li>The machine is supplied with a grounded cord and plug. Plug it into a matching grounded outlet; never modify the plug or use an adapter. Use only 3-wire extension cords. Inspect the cord regularly and have a damaged cord replaced by qualified personnel.</li>
        <li>Do not expose the machine to rain or use it in damp locations. If unavoidable, use a GFCI/RCD-protected supply.</li>
        <li>Always wear eye protection. Keep hair and loose clothing away from the wheels. Keep hands dry and free of grease and oil.</li>
        <li>Make sure the switch is off before plugging in. Unplug before changing wheels, making adjustments or storing the machine.</li>
        <li><strong>Keep your fingers out of the gap between the jig and the grinding wheel.</strong></li>
        <li>Use only Tormek original jigs, accessories and grinding wheels. Use only wheels intended for the T-8: max &oslash; 250 mm, max 50 mm wide, 12 mm bore.</li>
        <li>When using the universal support or the SVD-110 as a tool rest, the gap between the support and the stone must never exceed 2 mm. Re-adjust as the stone wears.</li>
        <li><strong>Free-hand grinding:</strong> grind with the wheel running away from the edge (edge trailing). <strong>Honing:</strong> always hone with the wheel running away from the edge. Honing into the edge will cut into the leather.</li>
        <li>Do not make adjustments until the wheel has stopped. Never leave the machine switched on unattended.</li>
        <li>Never leave a wet grinding wheel in freezing temperatures; a frozen, saturated stone can crack.</li>
        <li>Store the machine dry, unplugged and out of reach of children.</li>
        <li>Have the machine serviced only by a qualified repair person using identical replacement parts. Contact your Tormek dealer before returning a machine; most problems are solved by phone or by a spare part.</li>
      </ul>
